# EAS Build uploads a source archive of the project. android/ is a native,
# generated (fully .gitignore'd) project directory -- exclude its build
# output/intermediates explicitly so uploads don't try to touch files a
# concurrent local Gradle build has open (this caused a real EPERM failure
# from a Windows file lock), and so uploads aren't wasted on gigabytes of
# local build artifacts EAS recompiles from scratch server-side anyway.
android/app/build/
android/app/.cxx/
android/.gradle/
android/build/
node_modules/
